        <body>
            <div xml:id="d54-a1">

                <pb facs="0141" n="123" sameAs="frus:frus1902app1/pg123"/>

                <head>[Extract from deposition of Abial P. Loud, special assistant treasury agent on
                    Pribilof Islands.]</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">management and pelagic
                        sealing</hi>.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I examined the seal skins she had on board, and about 80 per cent were skins of
                    females. In 1888 or 1889 I examined something like 5,000 skins at Unalaska which
                    had been taken from schooners engaged in pelagic sealing in Bering Sea, and at
                    least 80 to 85 per cent were skins of females.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Abial P. Loud.</hi></signed></closer>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">Subscribed and sworn to before me, a notary
                        public in the <placeName>District of Columbia</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1892-04-15">this 15th day of April,
                            1892</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#small-caps">seal.</hi>] <signed><hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Chas. L. Hughes</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Notary Public.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
